+# Fixed retained-current Peer record, private proposal
+
+Status: implemented afterimages and six finite selectors, AST checked only.
+No owning execution, new public prefix, repository change or qualification.
+Basis is the frozen qualified RootIO15 packet, not either rejected runtime/lock
+optimization. Future owning execution must freshly pin the current clean HEAD.
+
+## Exact API and default
+
+One cold `FixedParentPeerScope(current_graphs=False)` option; True requires the
+already selected RootIO15 policies and records profile16. Omission preserves
+profile15, dictionary-valued record births and the conservative complete graphs.
+The helper module is imported/registered only for the new policy.
+
+`RetainedPeerGraphs` is strongly registered with the actual Archive birth tuple
+before constructor IO. It has no provider, arbitrary parser, SDK, generic
+allocator, resource pool or independent namespace. All original16MiB/512 and
+Parent4456448-byte/68-file forward reservation rules remain unchanged.
+
+`PeerGraphSlot` holds one original graph/seal and immutable
+`(peer,ordinal,originalRaw,originalReceipt,originalSealCapacity)` birth. Record
+birth retains this typed slot instead of a second direct graph reference. While
+open, the original exact graph/container edges remain freshly checked. Closed
+slots keep raw/ordinal/receipt/capacity but have graph/seal None. All raw bytes,
+parts and original physical/OFD custody remain. Default records remain dicts.
+An active graph getter is allowed only during the original typed Journey wait;
+a closed/outside-window getter refuses rather than redecoding or caching facts.
+
+## Actual closed caller boundary
+
+The original wait body is preserved, with one fixed pure marker immediately
+after its original `samples.append`. At that point:
+
+1. `poll_independent_witness`, strict decode/read/record and
+   `pico_peer_after_primary`/`observed_witness` helper frames actually returned.
+2. The wait frame already set `witness_original=None`.
+3. The wait frame retains the actual selected witness ENTRY and facts subtree,
+   which the original append just stored. It does not retain the full snapshot.
+4. Native value, evidence, navigation/report/cursor/cleanup roots remain. They
+   are not cleared or declared zero. The historical alias census remains the
+   basis; fixed original consumer methods and helper functions are source pinned.
+
+`prepare_poll_marker` prepares the fixed tuple BEFORE the original final
+freshness/clock checks. After the original append, `mark_poll_recorded` checks
+actual Native result/sample state/resources identity and commits only that
+preallocated pointer. It creates no new tuple/list/import and does NO IO, clock,
+parse, encoding, census or retirement. No allocating callback follows freshness.
+The fixed wait wrapper only bounds getter access and clears that access after
+the actual body returns. On any error it keeps the first TB/full current SUM.
+
+An expired-but-valid pair can be recorded as historical without qualifying;
+its original currentness result remains false. Hard parse/order/contradiction/
+receipt/source errors never reach the marker. There is no input replay, clock
+renewal, threshold change or current verdict cache.
+
+Actual retirement occurs only at the NEXT `historical_preview`, before the new
+poll_started anchor. It remains inside the original checkpoint20 seconds. The
+latest complete original snapshot stays active for all prefix/order/receipt/
+contradiction checks. Every selected witness outside that latest graph is held
+by exact identity in a separately sealed list. Witnesses already inside a kept
+full graph remain fully funded there. Every actual samples witness must belong
+to that escaped list or an active original graph. No expected facts are used.
+
+## Same-bank booking and actual return
+
+Before any closure allocation, all existing positive grants remain live. The
+fixed preheld constructor META covers at most512 reference slots and pure walks.
+Use actual `container_dimensions`/`canonical_size` to compute the entire new
+escaped-root extent, its seal construction peak and the actual Header seal peak.
+Original `_book` grants ALL of that alongside all old graphs/old escaped roots.
+
+Pending closure strongly holds every old graph/seal, prior escaped roots/seal,
+old Header, new actual roots/seal and exact lower Header BEFORE the original CAS.
+The original Root writer, RootIO work, full Archive guard and prospective _admit
+all run with full old+new charge. `charge = fullBefore - actualPeerHeld` keeps
+the exact unconfirmed difference through every held-field transition. It does
+not depend on a separately cleared boolean or loan future retired credit.
+
+Only after `_retire_body` really returns are older slot graph/seal pointers
+cleared. Pending still keeps all old payloads until the final pure store ends
+that holder and its charge together. Latest graph, raw bytes, all escaped
+witnesses, ledger, other grants and HTTP metadata remain. Any error/unknown
